---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { assets } from "../../content/assets";
import { tribe, links, profile } from "../../content/site";
---

<Base
  title="Tribe — case study"
  description="Inside Tribe: an AI-powered platform bringing business tools, commerce, and payments into one connected experience, with Tia on WhatsApp and the web."
  path="/work/tribe"
  ogType="article"
>
  <section class="page-head" data-theme="cream">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Currently building</p>
      <h1 class="display-1 page-head__title">
        Tribe helps people run business with less friction.
      </h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">{tribe.description}</p>
      <dl class="case-meta">
        <div>
          <dt>Role</dt>
          <dd>{tribe.role}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Status</dt>
          <dd>Live, in active development</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Site</dt>
          <dd><a class="inline-link" href={links.tribe} rel="noopener">usetribeapp.com</a></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cream" style="padding-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)">
    <div class="shell">
      <figure class="case-figure" data-reveal>
        <span class="media-frame">
          <Image
            src={assets.tribeWeb.src}
            alt={assets.tribeWeb.alt}
            widths={[720, 1080, 1440]}
            sizes="(min-width: 1240px) 72rem, 92vw"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </span>
        <figcaption>Screenshot of usetribeapp.com, captured 11 October 2026.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="prose-block case-body">
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>
          Running a small business usually means running several disconnected systems at
          once. Payments arrive in one place, customer questions land in a chat, the stock
          count lives in a notebook, and the record of who still owes money lives in
          someone's head. Nothing is broken on its own, but the owner spends the day
          stitching it together.
        </p>

        <h2>What Tribe is</h2>
        <p>
          Tribe brings those pieces into one connected experience. Products and services,
          inventory, orders, payment links, invoices, receipts, and customer follow-ups sit
          together, so the state of the business is visible in one place instead of five.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tia is the assistant layer on top. Instead of navigating menus, you ask: what
          needs my attention today? Tia can explain recorded activity, prepare documents
          and messages, set up reminders, and move a task along. It works on WhatsApp and
          on the web, so the conversation is available where the business already happens.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside the business tools, Tribe covers everyday money — bills, reminders, and
          payments — and adds marketplace mechanics such as escrow-protected orders, where
          payment is released once delivery is confirmed. Affiliates can opt in to promote
          eligible products and earn commission on qualifying sales.
        </p>

        <h2>My role</h2>
        <p>
          I am Tribe's founder and software developer. That covers the shape of the product
          — what it does, what it deliberately does not do yet — as well as the design and
          implementation work behind the interfaces people use.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it is going</h2>
        <p>{tribe.vision}</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="value-list case-values">
        {
          tribe.values.map((value) => (
            <li class="value case-value">
              <h3>{value.title}</h3>
              <p>{value.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="case-media">
        <figure data-reveal>
          <span class="media-frame tilt" style="--rot:1.5deg">
            <Image
              src={assets.tribeAppDesign.src}
              alt={assets.tribeAppDesign.alt}
              widths={[360, 540, 720]}
              sizes="(min-width: 900px) 20rem, 60vw"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </span>
          <figcaption>
            Tribe app interface design. Product design work with placeholder figures — not a
            screenshot of a live build.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:0.1s">
          <span class="media-frame tilt" style="--rot:-1.5deg">
            <Image
              src={assets.eventBanner.src}
              alt={assets.eventBanner.alt}
              widths={[420, 640]}
              sizes="(min-width: 900px) 22rem, 70vw"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </span>
          <figcaption>
            Showing Tribe at an exhibition — where most of the useful product feedback comes
            from.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="case-cta">
        <h2 class="display-3">Try it, or ask me about it.</h2>
        <div class="actions mt-1">
          <a class="pill pill--ink" href={links.tribe} rel="noopener">Visit Tribe</a>
          <a class="pill pill--ghost" href="/#contact">Talk to {profile.name.split(" ")[0]}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  }

  .case-meta div {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.14);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  .case-meta dt {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .case-meta dd {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .case-figure {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .case-figure figcaption,
  .case-media figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .case-body {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .case-values {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.14);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .case-value h3 {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-value p {
    color: rgba(20, 18, 17, 0.74);
  }

  .case-value {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .case-media {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .case-media figure {
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1 1 18rem;
    max-width: 24rem;
  }

  .case-cta {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.14);
  }
</style>
